                           Change Setup Help
                           -----------------


Here you may edit information about yourself, edit your password, and turn
colour ANSI graphics, expert mode and hot-keys on or off.

To edit something, simply press the corresponding key.  Please be truthful
when you are entering personnal information such as your phone number.

Your password can be any combination of characters, up to ten (10) characters
long.

In order to display ANSI graphics properly, you must be using a terminal
program capable of translating the ANSI Escape codes into colour.  Most Amiga
telecommunications programs do just that, as do most IBM ones, and some
Macintosh ones.  If your terminal is not capable of diplaying ANSI codes, you
will see things such as "[32m" in front of most text.

If you prefer "hot-keys" to the default command-stacking method of
selecting commands from menus, you can toggle hot-keys on.

If you do not wish to see the full menus displayed all the time, toggle
export mode on.

Press 'Q' to go back to the main menu.

